  "facts": [
    "The Robert F. Kennedy Bridge, once called the Triborough Bridge, opened in 1940 and was the world’s largest lift bridge at the time, spanning 310 feet with a 92‑foot wide deck.",
    "Its East River suspension span, designed by Othmar Ammann, stretches 2,780 feet, with main cables each 20 inches thick and containing 10,800 miles of individual wires.",
    "Built by Allston Dana and architect Aymar Embury II, the complex links Manhattan, Queens, and the Bronx across Randalls and Wards Islands, totaling 17.5 miles of roadway."
  ],
